+    {
+      "answer_id": 4874,
+      "language": "go",
+      "environment": "docker",
+      "version": "latest",
+      "solution": "Solution written to **`/workspace/SOLUTION.md`** and verified with a runnable harness.\n\n## Diagnosis\n\nTwo JSON shapes were conflated:\n\n| Input | Producer | Shape | Correct selector |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `classification.json` (current) | `jq -s` helper | bare **array** | `.[]` |\n| prior receipt | receipt writer | **object** | `.dirty_classification[]` |\n\nThe rapid-refire delta path applied the envelope selector `.dirty_classification[]` to the bare-array component file. `jq` fails with `Cannot index array with string \"dirty_classification\"` and exits **5**; under `set -euo pipefail` the builder dies before writing the receipt. Exit `5` collides with the script's own \"promoted path exists\" code, causing misattribution.\n\n## Fix\n\n- Current side (`$CLASSIFICATION_JSON`): `.dirty_classification[]` → `.[]`\n- Prior receipt side (`$PRIOR_RECEIPT`): keep `.dirty_classification[]`\n\nIncluded in the doc: the before/after snippet, a split-variables form, an optional `jq -e 'type==\"array\"'` guardrail, and distinct failure exit statuses so `jq` type errors can't masquerade as code `5`.\n\n## Verification (actually run)\n\n```\nBUGGY rc=5 err=jq: error (at .../classification.json:5): Cannot index array with string \"dirty_classification\"\ncurrent dirty:\nsrc/a.sh\nsrc/c.sh\nprior dirty:\nsrc/old.sh\ndelta:\nsrc/a.sh\nsrc/c.sh\nVERIFIED\n```\n\nThe harness reproduces the exact exit-5 error, then confirms the corrected selectors produce the right current/prior dirty sets and delta.\n",
+      "evidence": "# Evidence\n- Problem class: bash-jq-schema-array-vs-object-mismatch\n- Model: openrouter/deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash\n- Solved: 2026-11-03T10:05:39.921Z\n- Verification: solution produced by pi in sandbox; see signatures.json\n",
+      "signatures": {
+        "description": "build-monitoring-blocked-receipt.sh rapid-refire delta path queried .dirty_classification[] on classification.json, but that file is the bare classification ARRAY produced by jq -s (the receipt embeds it as $cls[0]). jq fails with 'Cannot index array with string \"dirty_classification\"' and exits 5, which under set -euo pipefail kills the builder before the receipt is built (exit code 5 is also the script's 'promoted path exists' code, so the failure is easy to misattribute). Fix: query '.[] | ...' on the bare array for the current side and keep '.dirty_classification[]' only for the prior RECEIPT side. General lesson: when a helper writes a component file (jq -s array) and a receipt envelope (object with named keys), never query both with the same selector.",
