+{
+  "class_id": 3140,
+  "title": "git-bare-rebase-head-proven-stale-classification",
+  "description": "git-bare-rebase-head-proven-stale-classification",
+  "created_at": "2026-11-03 10:19:28",
+  "answers": [
+    {
+      "answer_id": 4875,
+      "language": "shell",
+      "environment": "docker",
+      "version": "latest",
+      "solution": "Done. I produced a verified, self-contained solution.\n\n## Deliverables (in `~/work`)\n\n- **`SOLUTION.md`** — the markdown solution (title, root-cause analysis, exact fix, verification).\n- **`bin/rebase-head-probe.sh`** — the tested standalone probe (embedded verbatim in `SOLUTION.md`; extracted copy verified byte-identical and shellcheck-clean).\n- **`reproduce.sh`** — synthetic reproduction of the `<project>` scenario used to verify the fix.\n\n## Root cause\n\nTwo independent items were being collapsed into one \"blocked\" signal:\n\n1. **`REBASE_HEAD` is residue, not state.** Git leaves the bare marker after a finished rebase (crash/interruption). Authoritative state is `rebase-merge/`/`rebase-apply/`. The tick keys on the marker's mere existence, so completed residue looks active. `root-operation-gate.sh` checks real state and correctly reports `gate_violations=0` — which is exactly why the standalone probe must run *after* the gate.\n2. **`.vfs/graph/*` are hook-generated.** Repo-local `core.hooksPath` (`post-commit` → `hilo graph warm --changed`) rewrites them on every commit/merge, so they always look newer than the last commit and get flagged as an unknown writer.\n\n## Fix\n\nA standalone probe that classifies `PROVEN_STALE` only when all four agree: (1) marker mtime/content matches a `rebase (start)` reflog entry; (2) a `rebase (finish)` postdates it **and** later normal ops exist (remote `update by push` and/or new commits); (3) no rebase state dir in git-dir or common-dir; (4) a `timeout`-bounded exact-cwd `/proc` census finds no rebase owner (services/hung test binaries excluded). It also attributes the cache to the warmer hook and reports `tracked`/`staged`. The marker is recorded as residue and **never deleted**; cache stays untouched and unstaged.\n\n## Verification results\n\n| Case | Expected | Observed |\n|---|---|---|\n| Full stale scenario | `PROVEN_STALE` / exit 0 | ✅ |\n| `rebase-merge/` present | `ACTIVE` / exit 3 | ✅ |\n| Live `git rebase --continue` in tree | `ACTIVE` / exit 3 | ✅ |\n| No `rebase (finish)` | `INDETERMINATE` / exit 4 | ✅ |\n| No warmer hook | cache not attributed | ✅ |\n| `git add -f` a cache file | `tracked=true, staged=true` | ✅ |\n| Run twice | marker bytes/mtime unchanged | ✅ |\n| `shellcheck -S warning` | clean | ✅ |\n\nRun from the tick:\n\n```bash\ncd /path/to/<project>\nbash scripts/root-operation-gate.sh --json > .foreman/gate.json || true\nbash scripts/rebase-head-probe.sh --json > .foreman/rebase-probe.json   # always, even if gate_violations=0\n```\n\nProceed only when the probe exits `0`; fold `residue_note`/`unblock_menu`/`cache` into the receipt.\n",
+      "evidence": "# Evidence\n- Problem class: git-bare-rebase-head-proven-stale-classification\n- Model: openrouter/deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash\n- Solved: 2026-11-03T10:19:28.391Z\n- Verification: solution produced by pi in sandbox; see signatures.json\n",
+      "signatures": {
+        "description": "A bare .git/REBASE_HEAD marker plus untracked hook-generated cache files (.vfs/graph/*) repeatedly blocks foreman ticks on a repo whose rebase actually COMPLETED. Proven-stale classification recipe (all four must agree): (1) marker mtime/content matches a rebase (start) reflog entry; (2) a rebase (finish) entry postdates it AND later normal operations exist after the finish (check refs/remotes/<origin> reflog for 'update by push' entries and new commits — pushes count as later normal operations even when the local HEAD reflog is silent); (3) no rebase-merge/rebase-apply dir in git-dir or common-dir; (4) bounded exact-cwd process census finds no rebase owner (live services/hung test binaries with cwd in the tree are separate ownership items, not rebase owners). Proven-stale marker = residue to record in the receipt's residue_note/unblock_menu, never delete it; the tick may proceed. For the generated cache: read git config core.hooksPath, inspect post-commit/post-merge for cache warmers (e.g. hilo graph warm --changed), and correlate cache mtimes with the latest commit/merge/checkout hook fire — identified writer satisfies the ownership stop; keep the cache untouched and never staged. A stale REBASE_HEAD coexists with gate_violations=0 from root-operation-gate.sh, so always run the standalone bare-marker probe after the gate.",
+        "environment": "",
+        "language": "shell",
+        "model": "openrouter/deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash",
+        "problem_class": "git-bare-rebase-head-proven-stale-classification",
+        "provider": "openrouter",
+        "solved_at": "2026-11-03T10:19:28.391Z",
+        "version": ""
+      },
+      "status": "verified",
+      "created_at": "2026-11-03 10:19:28"
+    }
+  ]
