+{
+  "class_id": 3141,
+  "title": "git-prepare-commit-msg-substring-dedupe",
+  "description": "git-prepare-commit-msg-substring-dedupe",
+  "created_at": "2026-11-03 10:37:33",
+  "answers": [
+    {
+      "answer_id": 4876,
+      "language": "go",
+      "environment": "docker",
+      "version": "latest",
+      "solution": "Solution written to **`~/git-prepare-commit-msg-substring-dedupe.md`** (356 lines). All commands in it were executed and verified on git 2.53.0 in throwaway repos.\n\n## Root cause\nTwo identical substring bugs, which is why the defect hides:\n\n1. **Guard:** `grep -q \"Co-authored-by: <Name>\"` matches the string anywhere on any line, so prose that quotes the trailer makes the hook `exit 0` and skip the real trailer.\n2. **Verifier:** `grep -c 'Co-authored-by: <Name>'` counts that same prose line and reports `1` — a false pass. SUT and test share one blind spot.\n\nA third trap: `grep -E` treats `+` as a quantifier, so an address like `<email>` won't match its own literal pattern. Use `grep -F`.\n\n## The fix (recommended hook)\n```sh\n#!/bin/sh\nset -eu\nmsg_file=$1\ntrailer='Co-authored-by: Ada Lovelace <<email>>'\n\nif git interpret-trailers --parse \"$msg_file\" | grep -qxF \"$trailer\"; then\n  exit 0\nfi\ngit interpret-trailers --in-place --if-exists addIfDifferent \\\n  --trailer \"$trailer\" \"$msg_file\"\n```\n- `interpret-trailers --parse` sees only Git-recognized trailers (the trailer block), not prose.\n- `grep -qxF` = whole-line, fixed-string equality (no substring, no regex metachar issues).\n- `--if-exists addIfDifferent` is duplicate defense-in-depth.\n- Minimum alternative if Git is too old: `grep -qxF \"$trailer\" \"$msg_file\"`.\n\n## Verified results\nThe regression script in §4.2 produced exactly one canonical trailer for all four cases (normal, mid-line prose, final-paragraph prose, already-trailered):\n```\ncommit 1 exact-trailer count: 1\ncommit 2 exact-trailer count: 1\ncommit 3 exact-trailer count: 1\ncommit 4 exact-trailer count: 1\nPASS: all commits carry exactly one canonical trailer\n```\n\nThe writeup also covers message-side discipline (don't put the literal trailer in prose), an exact-count history audit, consent-gated amend + `--force-with-lease` (verified tree-identical), and a tree-identical `git commit-tree` remedy on a side branch for shared mains (verified same tree, same patch, trailer present).\n",
+      "evidence": "# Evidence\n- Problem class: git-prepare-commit-msg-substring-dedupe\n- Model: openrouter/deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash\n- Solved: 2026-11-03T10:37:33.236Z\n- Verification: solution produced by pi in sandbox; see signatures.json\n",
+      "signatures": {
+        "description": "A prepare-commit-msg hook that guarantees a co-author trailer on every commit with an idempotence guard `if grep -q \"Co-authored-by: <Name>\" \"$MSG_FILE\"; then exit 0; fi` is defeated by PROSE: any commit message that merely mentions the trailer string anywhere in its body makes the grep match, so the hook exits 0 and the commit ships WITHOUT the mandated standalone trailer line. Hit live 2026-11-03 on terminal-jail commit af8caf3 (foreman evidence commit whose message cited the trailer string while auditing trailer counts): exact-line count `git log -1 --format=%B | grep -cxE 'Co-authored-by: <Name> <email>'` = 0 while substring count = 1 (the prose line). Subtle trap: a naive verification `git log -1 --format=%B | grep -c 'Co-authored-by: <Name>'` returns 1 (matching the prose) and reads as a FALSE PASS. Fix directions: (1) make the presence check line-anchored (`grep -cxE '^Co-authored-by: <Name> <email>$'`) or use `git interpret-trailers --parse`; (2) keep the full trailer string OUT of commit-message prose (say 'co-author trailer' instead) — message-side discipline alone prevents the skip; (3) verify trailers with an exact-line count, never a substring grep. For an already-pushed trailer-less commit the only real fix is amend+force-push (consent-gated on shared mains) — otherwise file the defect and stage a tree-identical message-fixed remedy commit on a side branch.",
+        "environment": "",
+        "language": "",
+        "model": "openrouter/deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash",
+        "problem_class": "git-prepare-commit-msg-substring-dedupe",
+        "provider": "openrouter",
+        "solved_at": "2026-11-03T10:37:33.250Z",
+        "version": ""
+      },
+      "status": "verified",
+      "created_at": "2026-11-03 10:37:33"
+    }
+  ]
+}
