+      "solution": "Done. I diagnosed the problem, implemented a verified bounded-state verifier, and assembled the self-contained report.\n\n## Deliverables in `~`\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `ctap2_verifier.py` | The verifier (Ed25519 assertions, bounded state, clone/rollback detection) |\n| `test_ctap2_verifier.py` | 19-test suite covering every scenario |\n| `demo_fleet.py` | End-to-end fleet scenario |\n| `solution.md` | Full markdown report (title, root-cause analysis, exact fix with embedded code, verification) |\n\n## Root cause\n\nNaive verifiers compare each new counter to the **last delivered** event, so reordering/truncation/concurrency corrupt the baseline; they treat every reset as hostile though only a fresh **attested enrollment epoch** proves a legitimate reset; and they keep unbounded history to detect reuse. The key invariant is that a single device can never emit **the same counter with two different signed challenges** — that is a clone — while a counter falling below a tolerance window without reuse is rollback. Wall-clock time must never order events.\n\n## Fix (highlights)\n\n- Per `(authenticator, credential)`: `high_water`, bounded `seen` window `[hw-W, hw]`, bounded `recent counter→{challenges}`.\n- Bounded LRU dedup keyed by a timestamp-free semantic event id (idempotent under retransmit/skew).\n- Detection precedence: reused counter + new challenge → **CLONE**; unseen counter below window → **COUNTER_ROLLBACK**; gaps and in-window reordering → OK.\n- Resets accepted only via higher `epoch` + re-enrollment; late pre-reset events → benign `stale_epoch`; claimed reset without re-enrollment → `invalid_epoch`.\n- Rotation records signed by the prior key, validated at enrollment; rotations don't reset the counter.\n\n## Verification\n\n```\n$ python3 -m pytest test_ctap2_verifier.py -q\n...................                    [100%]\n19 passed in 0.75s\n\n$ python3 demo_fleet.py\n[main] {'processed': 8, 'attacks': 2, ... 'counter_rollback': 1, 'clone': 1 ...}\n[rotation] {'processed': 2, 'attacks': 0, ...}\n  ATTACK: counter_rollback - counter 0 below high-water 9 (window 8)\n  ATTACK: clone - counter 9 reused with new challenge (clone)\n```\n\nThe full report with all code and the property/coverage table is in `solution.md`.\n",
+      "evidence": "# Evidence\n- Problem class: python3-ctap2-counter-rollback-detection-20261102\n- Model: openrouter/deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash\n- Solved: 2026-11-03T10:58:08.263Z\n- Verification: solution produced by pi in sandbox; see signatures.json\n",
