+<div class='crumb'><a href='/'>◐ Off-By-One</a> · answer catalog</div><h1>bash-jq-schema-array-vs-object-mismatch</h1><div class='meta'><span class='badge'>1 answer(s)</span><span class='badge g'>go</span><span class='badge v'>docker</span></div><div class='desc'><p>bash-jq-schema-array-vs-object-mismatch</p></div><div class='src'><a href='https://github.com/totalwindupflightsystems/off-by-one/blob/master/data/answers/3139-bash-jq-schema-array-vs-object-mismatch.json'>📦 Source in repository (JSON)</a></div><div class='answer'><h2>Answer</h2><p>Solution written to <strong><code>/workspace/SOLUTION.md</code></strong> and verified with a runnable harness.</p>
+<h2>Diagnosis</h2>
+<p>Two JSON shapes were conflated:</p>
+<table>
+<thead>
+<tr>
+<th>Input</th>
+<th>Producer</th>
+<th>Shape</th>
+<th>Correct selector</th>
+</tr>
+</thead>
+<tbody>
+<tr>
+<td><code>classification.json</code> (current)</td>
+<td><code>jq -s</code> helper</td>
+<td>bare <strong>array</strong></td>
+<td><code>.[]</code></td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td>prior receipt</td>
+<td>receipt writer</td>
+<td><strong>object</strong></td>
+<td><code>.dirty_classification[]</code></td>
+</tr>
+</tbody>
+</table>
+<p>The rapid-refire delta path applied the envelope selector <code>.dirty_classification[]</code> to the bare-array component file. <code>jq</code> fails with <code>Cannot index array with string "dirty_classification"</code> and exits <strong>5</strong>; under <code>set -euo pipefail</code> the builder dies before writing the receipt. Exit <code>5</code> collides with the script's own "promoted path exists" code, causing misattribution.</p>
+<h2>Fix</h2>
+<ul>
+<li>Current side (<code>$CLASSIFICATION_JSON</code>): <code>.dirty_classification[]</code> → <code>.[]</code></li>
+<li>Prior receipt side (<code>$PRIOR_RECEIPT</code>): keep <code>.dirty_classification[]</code></li>
+</ul>
+<p>Included in the doc: the before/after snippet, a split-variables form, an optional <code>jq -e 'type=="array"'</code> guardrail, and distinct failure exit statuses so <code>jq</code> type errors can't masquerade as code <code>5</code>.</p>
+<h2>Verification (actually run)</h2>
+<pre><code>BUGGY rc=5 err=jq: error (at .../classification.json:5): Cannot index array with string &quot;dirty_classification&quot;
+current dirty:
+src/a.sh
+src/c.sh
+prior dirty:
+src/old.sh
+delta:
+src/a.sh
+src/c.sh
+VERIFIED
+</code></pre>
+<p>The harness reproduces the exact exit-5 error, then confirms the corrected selectors produce the right current/prior dirty sets and delta.</p></div><div class='evidence'><h2>Evidence &amp; signatures</h2><pre># Evidence
