+<div class='crumb'><a href='/'>◐ Off-By-One</a> · answer catalog</div><h1>git-bare-rebase-head-proven-stale-classification</h1><div class='meta'><span class='badge'>1 answer(s)</span><span class='badge g'>shell</span><span class='badge v'>docker</span></div><div class='desc'><p>git-bare-rebase-head-proven-stale-classification</p></div><div class='src'><a href='https://github.com/totalwindupflightsystems/off-by-one/blob/master/data/answers/3140-git-bare-rebase-head-proven-stale-classification.json'>📦 Source in repository (JSON)</a></div><div class='answer'><h2>Answer</h2><p>Done. I produced a verified, self-contained solution.</p>
+<h2>Deliverables (in <code>~/work</code>)</h2>
+<ul>
+<li><strong><code>SOLUTION.md</code></strong> — the markdown solution (title, root-cause analysis, exact fix, verification).</li>
+<li><strong><code>bin/rebase-head-probe.sh</code></strong> — the tested standalone probe (embedded verbatim in <code>SOLUTION.md</code>; extracted copy verified byte-identical and shellcheck-clean).</li>
+<li><strong><code>reproduce.sh</code></strong> — synthetic reproduction of the <code>&amp;lt;project&amp;gt;</code> scenario used to verify the fix.</li>
+</ul>
+<h2>Root cause</h2>
+<p>Two independent items were being collapsed into one "blocked" signal:</p>
+<ol>
+<li><strong><code>REBASE_HEAD</code> is residue, not state.</strong> Git leaves the bare marker after a finished rebase (crash/interruption). Authoritative state is <code>rebase-merge/</code>/<code>rebase-apply/</code>. The tick keys on the marker's mere existence, so completed residue looks active. <code>root-operation-gate.sh</code> checks real state and correctly reports <code>gate_violations=0</code> — which is exactly why the standalone probe must run <em>after</em> the gate.</li>
+<li><strong><code>.vfs/graph/*</code> are hook-generated.</strong> Repo-local <code>core.hooksPath</code> (<code>post-commit</code> → <code>hilo graph warm --changed</code>) rewrites them on every commit/merge, so they always look newer than the last commit and get flagged as an unknown writer.</li>
+</ol>
+<h2>Fix</h2>
+<p>A standalone probe that classifies <code>PROVEN_STALE</code> only when all four agree: (1) marker mtime/content matches a <code>rebase (start)</code> reflog entry; (2) a <code>rebase (finish)</code> postdates it <strong>and</strong> later normal ops exist (remote <code>update by push</code> and/or new commits); (3) no rebase state dir in git-dir or common-dir; (4) a <code>timeout</code>-bounded exact-cwd <code>/proc</code> census finds no rebase owner (services/hung test binaries excluded). It also attributes the cache to the warmer hook and reports <code>tracked</code>/<code>staged</code>. The marker is recorded as residue and <strong>never deleted</strong>; cache stays untouched and unstaged.</p>
+<h2>Verification results</h2>
